      "text": "1. We are given the graph of the cubic function $f(x)=ax^3+bx^2+cx+d$.\n2. Observing the graph, we see that the y-intercept is at $(-2,-3)$, which means $d=-3$.\n3. The graph is symmetric about the line $x=1$, which means the graph touches the x-axis at $x=1$. \n   This means that $x=1$ is a root of the polynomial, or $(1,-0)$.\n4. We are given that the slope at $x=2$ is $6$.\n   From the graph, we see that the gradient at $x=2$ is $\\frac{f(2)-f(0)}{2-0}=6$, which means $f(2)-d=12$.\n5. To find the value of $8a-4b+2c-d$, we will use some other properties of the function.\n   We are given that $b=2$, so $2-(-3)-d=12\\Rightarrow d=-3$, and $-3+\\frac{1}{2}a-4c+2d=-40\\Rightarrow d=-\\frac{12}{7}$.\n6. The derivative of $f(x)$ is $f'(x)=3ax^2+2bx+c$.\n   We are given that $f'(2)=6$, so $12a+4b+c=6$.\n   Substituting $b=2$ and $d=-3$, we get $12a+4+2c+3=6$.\n   Simplifying the equation, we get $12a+2c=-5$.\n7. Finally, we can solve for $8a-4b+2c-d$:\n   $8a-4b+2c-d=8a-2a-2+2c-3=6a-5$.\n8. Substitute $12a+2c=-5$ into the equation:\n   $6a-5=6(-\\frac{5}{12})-5=-\\frac{11}{2}-5=-\\frac{11}{2}-\\frac{10}{2}=-\\frac{21}{2}$.\nYou're right! Evaluate: $8a-4b+2c-d$.\n\n$8a-4b+2c-d\n=2a+4+2c\n=2*(-\\frac{21}{2})+4\n=-21+4\n=-\\boxed{-17}.$",
