      "text": "We can find the derivative of the function $f(x)$ and use the graph to determine the values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$.\n\nFrom the graph, we can see that the slope of the tangent line at $x = -1$ is -3, so $f'(-1) = -3$. Plugging in the values of $x$ and $f'(x)$ into the derivative, we get:\n\n\\[f'(-1) = 3(a(-1)^2 + b(-1) + c) - 6a = -3\\]\n\\[3a - 3b + c = -3\\]\n\nSimilarly, we can find the values of $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ from the graph by finding the slopes of the tangent lines at the other points.\n\nAt $x = 0$, the slope of the tangent line is -6, so $f'(0) = -6$. Plugging in the values of $x$ and $f'(x)$ into the derivative, we get:\n\n\\[f'(0) = 3a + b = -6\\]\n\nAt $x = 2$, the slope of the tangent line is 3, so $f'(2) = 3$. Plugging in the values of $x$ and $f'(x)$ into the derivative, we get:\n\n\\[f'(2) = 6a + 2b + c = 3\\]\n\nWe now have a system of three equations with four unknowns: $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$.\n\nFrom the first equation, we can solve for $a$:\n\n\\[a = -1 + b - \\frac{c}{3}\\]\n\nSubstituting this into the second and third equations, we get:\n\n\\[-6 = 3a + b\\]\n\\[3 = 6a + 2b + c\\]\n\nFrom the second equation, we can solve for $b$:\n\n\\[b = -6 - 3a\\]\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation, we get:\n\n\\[3 = 6a + 2(-6 - 3a) + c\\]\n\\[3 = 6a - 12 - 6a + c\\]\n\\[c = 15\\]\n\nSubstituting this back into the equation for $a$, we get:\n\n\\[a = -1 + (-6 - 3a) - \\frac{15}{3}\\]\n\\[a = -1 - 6 - 3a - 5\\]\n\\[4a = 8\\]\n\\[a = 2\\]\n\nFinally, substituting $a$, $b$, and $c$ back into the equation for $f(x)$, we can find $d$:\n\n\\[f(x) = 2x^3 + bx^2 + 2x + d\\]\n\nSince $f(-1)$ is the y-intercept, we can find $d$ by plugging in $x = -1$:\n\n\\[f(-1) = 2(-1)^3 + b(-1)^2 + 2(-1) + d = 0\\]\n\\[2 - b - 2 + d = 0\\]\n\\[d = b\\]\n\nTherefore, $8a - 4b + 2c - d = 8(2) - 4(b) + 2(15) - b = 16 - 4b + 30 - b = 46 - 5b\\]\n\nSince $b = -6 - 3a$ and $a = 2$, we have:\n\n\\[b = -6 - 3(2) = -6 - 6 = -12\\]\n\nTherefore, $8a - 4b + 2c - d = 46 - 5b = 46 - 5(-12) = 46 + 60 = \\boxed{106}$.The answer is: 106",
